        "original_id": "3e35ef21-5743-55ed-9e63-b6a8b96fac0b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sharon Gless, Ron Cowen, Daniel Lipman, Tony Jonas, Robert Fuest, David Wiltse, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, Audra Lindley\n- Products: Switch, Cagney & Lacey, The Trials of Rosie O'Neill, Queer as Folk, Burn Notice, Revenge of the Stepford Wives\n- Roles: Maggie Philbin, Sgt. Christine Cagney, Debbie Novotny, Madeline Westen\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n\nFacts:\n- Sharon Gless was born on May 31, 1943, and she is an American actress of stage, film, and television.\n- Sharon Gless played Maggie Philbin on \"Switch\" from 1975 to 1978.\n- Sharon Gless played Sgt. Christine Cagney in \"Cagney & Lacey\" from 1982 to 1988.\n- \"Revenge of the Stepford Wives\" was directed by Robert Fuest, written by David Wiltse, and starred Sharon Gless, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, and Audra Lindley.\n- Sharon Gless played the title role in \"The Trials of Rosie O'Neill\" from 1990 to 1992.\n- \"Queer as Folk\" was developed and written by Ron Cowen and Daniel Lipman, who also served as showrunners and executive producers.\n- Tony Jonas, a former President of Warner Bros., was also an executive producer of \"Queer as Folk.\"\n- Sharon Gless played Debbie Novotny in the Showtime cable television series \"Queer as Folk\" from 2000 to 2005.\n- Sharon Gless played Madeline Westen on \"Burn Notice\" from 2007 to 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
